_I_n_t_r_o_d_u_c_t_i_o_n


Uucp is a series of programs designed to  permit  communica-

tion  between  UNIX  systems using either dial-up, hardwired

communication or network communication lines.   It  is  used

for  file transfers and remote command execution.  The first

versions of the system were designed and implemented  by  M.

E. Lesk.819 Quite extensive corrections and improvements  were

made  by  Tom  Truscott, amongst others, from the net.  This

paper describes the current (second) implementation  of  the

UKUUCP system.


Uucp is a batch type operation.   Files  are  created  in  a

spool  directory  for  processing by the uucp demons.  There

are three types of files used for the execution of work.


_D_a_t_a _f_i_l_e_s contain data  for  transfer  to  remote  systems.

_W_o_r_k _f_i_l_e_s  contain  directions  for  file transfers between

systems.  _E_x_e_c_u_t_i_o_n _f_i_l_e_s are directions  for  UNIX  command

executions  which  involve the resources of one or more sys-

tems.


The uucp system consists of four primary and five  secondary

programs.  The primary programs are:


     uucp      This program creates work  and  gathers  data

