     ?_e_x_p_e_c_t

     !_a_l_t-_s_e_n_d


     (This is different from the old format but a program is

     provided to convert between the two.) Strings preceeded

     by a colon are sent to the remote sytem,  so  ":uucp\r"

     would send the string "uucp" then a return.


     Strings preceeded by a question mark are  searched  for

     on  the  input from the line.  In an _e_x_p_e_c_t string '\?'

     will match any character.  If it  succeeds  in  finding

     the  specified  string it will skip past all subsequent

     _a_l_t-_s_e_n_d or _e_x_p_e_c_t fields to the next _s_e_n_d field or the

     end of the login script.


